    "mf-auto-2029": "How to add block type materials",
    "mf-auto-2030": "1. Creating Geometry",
    "mf-auto-2031": "a. Check the size of the block you want to add.",
    "mf-auto-2032": "Example: Adding a block with Width 12mm, Height 14mm, and Depth 18mm.",
    "mf-auto-2033": "b. Open [Blank type settings]. (Shortcut: F6)",
    "mf-auto-2034": "c. Create a new block geometry under the [Geometries] tab.",
    "mf-auto-2035": "Referring to existing geometries will be helpful.",
    "mf-auto-2036": "d. Click the [New] button.",
    "mf-auto-2037": "e. Enter all required values.",
    "mf-auto-830": "English and numbers only!",
    "mf-auto-3000": "Enter the [Name]. (",
    "mf-auto-2040": "Enter [Height], [Width], and [Depth] according to the size.",
    "mf-auto-3001": "Enter the [+/-] value.",
    "mf-auto-2043": "Click the [Apply] button.",
    "mf-auto-2044": "2. Creating the Blank",
    "mf-auto-2045": "a. Go to the [Blank types] tab and create a block blank. (You can copy and utilize an existing block.)",
    "mf-auto-2046": "Click the [Edit] button.",
    "mf-auto-2047": "Enter the [Name]. (English and numbers only.)",
    "mf-auto-2048": "Set the [Geometry] to the shape you just created.",
    "mf-auto-2049": "Appropriately configure the remaining settings under the [Data] section. (If copied, keep existing values.)",
    "mf-auto-2050": "b. Close [Blank type settings].",
    "mf-auto-2051": "3. Linking the created blank to the fixture",
    "mf-auto-2052": "a. Open [Machining settings]. (Shortcut: F5)",
    "mf-auto-2053": "b. Select the appropriate jig in the [Fixtures] tab.",
    "mf-auto-2054": "For block materials, you must select the block jig ([MillFix-block]).",
    "mf-auto-2055": "c. On the [Filtering] tab on the right,",
    "mf-auto-2056": "Verify that the shape you just created is checked under [Blank geometry].",
    "mf-auto-2057": "If it is not checked, please check it.",
