    "mf-auto-2160": "Connector detail setting screen",
    "mf-auto-849": ": This is the number of connectors generated when set to automatic mode.",
    "mf-auto-2162": "Group size comparison: Group size 2 vs Group size 3",
    "mf-auto-851": "④ Milling cut",
    "mf-auto-852": ": This menu is for how much to trim when cutting the connector.",
    "mf-auto-2164": "Example of 40% milling cut and appearance after cutting the connector",
    "mf-auto-854": "⑤ Material",
    "mf-auto-855": ": You can select the material to which the setting will be applied. You can also set it as the default for a specific material.",
    "mf-auto-2166": "2. Saving Customized Connector Settings",
    "mf-auto-2167": "This is how to save customized settings.",
    "mf-auto-2168": "After saving, you can check it in the connector menu. The changed setting is applied.",
    "mf-auto-2169": "3. Auto connector setting",
    "mf-auto-2170": "Pressing F5 brings up the \"Machine settings\" menu.",
    "mf-auto-858": "In that menu, go to ",
    "mf-auto-859": ", then select the fixture type.",
    "mf-auto-3016": "Set \\'Allow overlapping~\\' to No and \\'Connectors adding to part\\' to Yes. Connectors are attached automatically when you nest the STL file on the blank.",
    "mf-auto-3017": "Conversely, if set to Yes and No respectively, connectors will not be attached automatically.",
    "mf-auto-2174": "4. Traverse",
    "mf-auto-3018": "What is Traverse? A feature where a connector bridges across prostheses with overlapping milling areas.",
    "mf-auto-3019": "Press the F5 key and set the Create Traverse option to Yes.",
    "mf-auto-2177": "After that, clicking the prosthesis in automatic mode will attach the connector crossing others.",
    "mf-auto-2178": "In manual mode, you can use the traverse function by clicking this button.",
    "mf-auto-3020": "5. Recommended connector by situation",
    "mf-auto-3021": "① Circle connector: Used in most situations. Set the milling cut low or to 0% when milling Zirconia.",
    "mf-auto-3022": "② Ellips connector: Used when the space to attach the connector is narrow.",
    "mf-auto-3023": "③ Oval Connector: Used when the space to attach the connector is narrow.",
    "mf-auto-3024": "6. Tip for setting connector",
    "mf-auto-3025": "If the location you want to attach the connector is a margin or an area where the upper prosthesis will contact, and it is difficult to avoid:",
    "mf-auto-3026": "Pressing Ctrl creates a virtual wall, allowing the connector to slide up/down along it to avoid sensitive areas.",
    "mf-auto-3027": "How to mill long screw channel over 15mm",
    "mf-auto-3028": "1. Requirements",
    "mf-auto-3029": "① hyperDENT version 10.1.1 or higher",
    "mf-auto-3030": "hyperDENT version can be checked by pressing the F12 key on the keyboard.",
    "mf-auto-3031": "② MAI DB(database) 251115 or higher",
